{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.101.8.a001", "note": "Retained the distributive core Morning by morning and its noun head after removing the article. The repeated English expresses the schedule jointly; the existing internal treatment of the preposition and repetition is preserved.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.101.8.001", "WLC.PSA.101.8.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.101.8.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.101.8.a002", "note": "The assimilated article has no corresponding determiner. Morning by morning names a recurring schedule rather than the definite temporal referent required by rule 30's article-inclusive adverb exception.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.101.8.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.101.8.002", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.101.8.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.101.8.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.101.8.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.101.8.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.101.8.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.101.8.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.101.8.a005", "note": "Anarthrous substantival adjective takes the supplied 'the' (rule 46).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.101.8.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.101.8.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.101.8.a006", "note": "Rectum takes 'of'; supplied 'the' is the noun's (rules 15, 19).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.101.8.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.101.8.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.101.8.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.101.8.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.101.8.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PSA.101.8.a008", "note": "'cut off' is one lexical verb plus particle; head on the verb (rule 44).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.101.8.009"], "source